  m_text: "Between the 8th and 18th centuries India was shaped by powerful regional kingdoms such as the Rashtrakutas, Cholas and Rajputs, by the Delhi Sultanate from 1206, by the Vijayanagara empire in the south and by the Mughals from 1526. Temples, mosques, tombs and forts of this age \u2013 and the devotional poetry of Bhakti and Sufi saints \u2013 remain among India's greatest cultural treasures."
