  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 301</b></color></size>

    <b>Brihadisvara Temple, Thanjavur</b>

    <size=74%>Completed 1010 CE

    <i>Granite; tower about 66 m high</i>

    In situ, Thanjavur, Tamil Nadu (UNESCO World Heritage Site)</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    Raja Raja I, the great Chola emperor, built this temple to Shiva at his capital Thanjavur. Its tower rises about 66 metres and is crowned by a huge granite capstone. Inscriptions on its walls list the gifts, dancers, musicians and staff that served the temple.</size>'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 723364797c8904a93956dad57186ed9d, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 3495093604678870679, guid: 723364797c8904a93956dad57186ed9d, type: 2}
