  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 310</b></color></size>

    <b>A wheel of the Sun Temple, Konark (replica)</b>

    <size=74%>c. 1250 CE

    <i>Replica of carved stone, about 3 m across</i>

    Replica made for this museum</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    King Narasimhadeva I of the Eastern Ganga dynasty built the Sun Temple at Konark as a giant stone chariot for the sun god Surya, drawn by seven horses on 24 carved wheels. Each wheel is about three metres across, and the shadows of its spokes can be read like a sundial.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Replica made for this museum</color></size>'
