  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 303</b></color></size>

    <b>Qutb Minar, Delhi</b>

    <size=74%>Begun c. 1199; completed 14th century

    <i>Red and buff sandstone and marble; about 72.5 m high</i>

    In situ, Delhi (UNESCO World Heritage Site)</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    Qutb-ud-din Aibak, founder of the Delhi Sultanate, began this victory tower beside the first mosque of Delhi; his successor Iltutmish added storeys, and Firuz Shah Tughlaq rebuilt the top in the 14th century. About 72.5 metres tall, it is carved with bands of Arabic inscriptions.</size>'
